# ============================================================================
# Snakefile_dog10k: DOG on the current assembly Dog10K_Boxer_Tasha: COUNTS ONLY
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Same 22 SRA libraries as Snakefile_dog (CanFam3.1), counted against the newest
# releases of Ensembl and RefSeq for the Dog10K_Boxer_Tasha assembly. No
# differential expression / fragility (COUNTS_ONLY); the pipeline stops at
#   results/per_annotation/dog10k/counts/<ann>/all_samples.counts.tsv
#
#   ensembl : Ensembl 112, Canis_lupus_familiarisboxer.Dog10K_Boxer_Tasha
#             (genome toplevel FASTA + GTF)
#   refseq  : NCBI RefSeq GCF_000002285.5 (Annotation Release 106)
#             (genome FASTA + GTF, native NC_/NW_ names)
# Every annotation on its own database's genome, no chromosome renaming.
#
# Mapping and counting exactly as in Snakefile_dog , so the
# two dog runs differ only in assembly + annotation:
#   STAR 2.5.3a, genome-only index, splice junctions from the GTF inserted at
#   mapping (--sjdbGTFfile, overhang 100), untrimmed reads;
#   featureCounts paired (-p --countReadPairs), -s 2 -O -M -t exon -g gene_id.
# Requires star_index_mode: per_annotation.
# Run   :  snakemake -s Snakefile_dog10k --profile profiles/slurm
# ============================================================================

